# AI-hint: Defines fapolicyd execution whitelist carve-outs for the MiOS agent's coderun sandbox, permitting execution of model-generated scripts within the isolated /var/home/mios/coderuns and .coderun-snapshots paths.
# AI-related: mios-agent-codegen, mios-deny
# /usr/lib/fapolicyd/rules.d/80-mios-agent-codegen.rules
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WS-7 -- fapolicyd execution-whitelist CARVE-OUT for the MiOS agent's
# legitimate sandboxed code generation / dry-run path.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# fapolicyd in enforce mode denies execution of any binary/script whose path
# is not trusted (RPM-db-backed or fs-verity-trusted). The MiOS agent stack
# deliberately writes + runs model-generated code in the coderun sandbox (see
# usr/share/doc/mios/concepts/coderun-sandbox.md): a rootless-podman,
# Network=none, DropCapability=ALL, seccomp-confined container whose /work +
# /tmp are the ONLY writable surfaces. Without an explicit allow, enforce-mode
# fapolicyd would deny the sandbox's interpreter from running the generated
# script -- breaking the one place the agent is *supposed* to execute untrusted
# code. This carve-out re-permits exec INSIDE that already-isolated boundary
# without re-opening the whole host.
#
# ORDERING: numbered 80- so it is evaluated BEFORE the 90-mios-deny.rules
# deny-by-default block (fapolicyd rules.d are read lexicographically; first
# match wins). It is INTENTIONALLY scoped to the sandbox roots only, so it
# never broadens execution on the operator's real home or system paths.
#
# SAFETY: these allows are INERT while fapolicyd is permissive (the WS-7
# default). They only take effect after the operator completes the documented
# permissive->enforce promotion. Keeping them in tree now means the carve-out
# is already present + reviewed before enforce is ever considered -- you do NOT
# want to discover a missing codegen allow by bricking a boot.
#
# PATHS: the sandbox workspace + snapshot roots resolve from mios.toml
# [paths].coderun_workspace_root / .coderun_snapshots_root (default
# /var/home/mios/coderuns and /var/home/mios/.coderun-snapshots). fapolicyd
# rules do not interpolate mios.toml, so these dir= globs are rendered by the
# WS-7 build step (automation/lib/ws7-uki-fapolicyd-build.sh) from the SSOT.
# The values below are the documented DEFAULTS; the build step rewrites them
# in place if the operator overrides the paths. The container runtime root
# (/var/lib/containers/) is already allowed by 70-bootc-ostree.rules; this file
# adds only the writable workspace surfaces the sandbox actually exec()s from.
#
# GRAMMAR (corrected 2026-06-04): fapolicyd puts SUBJECT attrs (uid/gid/trust/
# exe) LEFT of the colon and OBJECT attrs (dir/path/ftype) RIGHT -- so the form
# is `allow perm=execute all : dir=<path>` (cf. 70-bootc-ostree.rules
# `allow perm=any all : dir=/sysroot/...`). The earlier `dir=... : all` form was
# INVERTED -> fagenrules would reject it or it would never match -> codegen
# DENIED at enforce (the exact brick this carve-out exists to prevent).
#
# VALIDATE BEFORE ENFORCE (design review): model code runs INSIDE the rootless-
# podman coderun container; its interpreter lives in container storage under
# /var/lib/containers/ (already allowed by 70-bootc-ostree.rules), NOT at
# /var/home/. The HOST fapolicyd may not intercept in-container exec at all -- in
# which case these host /var/home allows are UNNECESSARY and re-open an exec
# surface 90-mios-deny deliberately closes (deny all trust=0 under /var/home).
# Confirm where exec actually originates; prefer to REMOVE these allows if the
# sandbox interpreter is container-trusted. INERT until enforce regardless.

# --- Sandboxed agent codegen: writable workspace + snapshots (carve-out) ---
allow perm=execute all : dir=/var/home/mios/coderuns/
allow perm=execute all : dir=/var/home/mios/.coderun-snapshots/

# --- Sandbox scratch (model dry-runs land scripts under the AI scratch dir) ---
# Resolves from mios.toml [paths].ai_scratch_dir (default below). Scoped to the
# scratch root only -- not /var/lib/mios at large.
allow perm=execute all : dir=/var/lib/mios/ai/scratch/
